<report>
<line><title>Sample size for survival analysis</title></line>
<line></line>
<line>median survival time for controls = <in>ctFmt</in></line>
<line>hazard ratio = <in>hrFmt</in></line>
<line>accrual time for recruitment = <in>atFmt</in></line>
<line>additional follow-up time after recruitment = <in>futFmt</in></line>
<line>alpha = <in>alpha</in></line>
<line>power = <in>power</in></line>
<line></line>
<line>Estimated minimum sample size = <in>size</in> experimental subjects and <in>controls</in> controls<block name="assumptions"></line>
<line></line>
<line><warn>NB:Assumptions of this calculation may cause over estimation of sample size when power is low.  However, true power associated with <in>cases</in> cases will be no less than <in>no_less</in> and no greater than <in>no_greater</in>.</warn></block></line>
<line></line>
<line></line>
</report>
